{"authored" [{"question" "q-34115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "20d19472c69d9ebe72c51149f2e67d4582e20538b94c07c37b848fd6ae4c3cc8" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-34115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}=-2 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 31\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=31,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $b$ does *not* lie in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "20d19472c69d9ebe72c51149f2e67d4582e20538b94c07c37b848fd6ae4c3cc8" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-34115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3c35d84f998953d540a017972af24b5f6997aadabed4c51265d82f0b6cbcbbfc" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-34115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "20d19472c69d9ebe72c51149f2e67d4582e20538b94c07c37b848fd6ae4c3cc8" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-34115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "20d19472c69d9ebe72c51149f2e67d4582e20538b94c07c37b848fd6ae4c3cc8" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-34115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "20d19472c69d9ebe72c51149f2e67d4582e20538b94c07c37b848fd6ae4c3cc8" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-34115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "20d19472c69d9ebe72c51149f2e67d4582e20538b94c07c37b848fd6ae4c3cc8" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-34115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "20d19472c69d9ebe72c51149f2e67d4582e20538b94c07c37b848fd6ae4c3cc8" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-34115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "20d19472c69d9ebe72c51149f2e67d4582e20538b94c07c37b848fd6ae4c3cc8" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105208" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "20d19472c69d9ebe72c51149f2e67d4582e20538b94c07c37b848fd6ae4c3cc8" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105208" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=-17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -5 & -17\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+3(-2)=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=9.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{a}_{1}+(-2){a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 9\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+(-2)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=9\\cdot (-2)=-18.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "20d19472c69d9ebe72c51149f2e67d4582e20538b94c07c37b848fd6ae4c3cc8" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105208" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3c35d84f998953d540a017972af24b5f6997aadabed4c51265d82f0b6cbcbbfc" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105208" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "20d19472c69d9ebe72c51149f2e67d4582e20538b94c07c37b848fd6ae4c3cc8" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105208" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-18"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "20d19472c69d9ebe72c51149f2e67d4582e20538b94c07c37b848fd6ae4c3cc8" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105208" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-27"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "20d19472c69d9ebe72c51149f2e67d4582e20538b94c07c37b848fd6ae4c3cc8" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105208" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-9"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "20d19472c69d9ebe72c51149f2e67d4582e20538b94c07c37b848fd6ae4c3cc8" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105208" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "16"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "20d19472c69d9ebe72c51149f2e67d4582e20538b94c07c37b848fd6ae4c3cc8" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105208" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/state.json" "file_sha256" "20d19472c69d9ebe72c51149f2e67d4582e20538b94c07c37b848fd6ae4c3cc8" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4795" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine if $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\},$ where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/assets/df4f126da2ab3a0661bcb7dc18bb1e5eae8cd48d5c5a1464ea580ccc439195d6.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/example-4795.json" "file_sha256" "3e19b0f0c7dc67e6b567ea672789a621d45843a2244810c763d7c81cb79caef7" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4795" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}$ if there exist $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=8 \\\\ {x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -21\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -21\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+8{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0x_1 + 0x_2 = 3,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $\\mathbf{b}$ does *not* lie in $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/example-4795.json" "file_sha256" "3e19b0f0c7dc67e6b567ea672789a621d45843a2244810c763d7c81cb79caef7" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\},$ where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/assets/966d2d7cd1cd0ef04a1d9b2adc04511dea86cbbf254166988a7072e952879fe0.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/example-6218.json" "file_sha256" "7f551d979a6417be2f07b40766826c373801e6d87004c1d9f5c5a727577d813c" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}$ if there exist $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=13 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ 7{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 2 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 14 & -70 \\\\ 7 & 2 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 14 & -70 \\\\ 0 & 16 & k-91\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{14}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 16 & k-91\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-16{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0x_1 + 0x_2 = k-11$. Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0 = k-11 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad k=11.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/example-6218.json" "file_sha256" "7f551d979a6417be2f07b40766826c373801e6d87004c1d9f5c5a727577d813c" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine if the vector $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\;\\Pi \\,:\\, \\mathbf{r}=s \\mathbf{b} + t \\mathbf{c}, \\, t,s \\in \\mathbb{R},$ where  $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 1, 4, 5 \\rangle, \\mathbf{c} = \\langle 2, 4, 6 \\rangle$ and  $\\mathbf{u}= \\langle 2, 10, 12 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/example-4799.json" "file_sha256" "e140477fcf0adf115d2f2c51e9814055491c3372f88f6c15241dc186e5220262" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By definition, $\\mathbf{u} \\in \\Pi$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s+2t=2 \\\\ 4s+4t=10 \\\\ 5s+6t=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 10 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s+2t=2 \\\\ -4t=2 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-4t = 2 \\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad t = -\\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s+2t & =2 \\\\ s+2(-\\frac{1}{2}) & =2 \\\\ s-1 & =2 \\\\ s & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=3, \\, t=-\\dfrac{1}{2},$ we conclude that $\\mathbf{u}$ does indeed lie on the plane $\\Pi.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}=3\\mathbf{b} - \\dfrac{1}{2}\\mathbf{c}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/example-4799.json" "file_sha256" "e140477fcf0adf115d2f2c51e9814055491c3372f88f6c15241dc186e5220262" "basis" 1634 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043954/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-34117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, ${a}_{3}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce26831e23d08765ee5e6e3107cbde1d08ad88c5819e10d9cafe4dcac9a02e19" "basis" 2103 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-34117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+6{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-9 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 18 & -21 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-18{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+6{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+6(-1)=-4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+(-3){a}_{2}+(-1){a}_{3} & =b \\\\ 2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+(-3)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+(-1)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=2\\cdot (-3)\\cdot (-1)=6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce26831e23d08765ee5e6e3107cbde1d08ad88c5819e10d9cafe4dcac9a02e19" "basis" 2103 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-34117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7604223d1ff525b3348731edda4438ac95858e98d15977ecd0b503cd9c307c0e" "basis" 2103 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-34117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce26831e23d08765ee5e6e3107cbde1d08ad88c5819e10d9cafe4dcac9a02e19" "basis" 2103 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-34117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce26831e23d08765ee5e6e3107cbde1d08ad88c5819e10d9cafe4dcac9a02e19" "basis" 2103 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-34117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce26831e23d08765ee5e6e3107cbde1d08ad88c5819e10d9cafe4dcac9a02e19" "basis" 2103 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-34117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce26831e23d08765ee5e6e3107cbde1d08ad88c5819e10d9cafe4dcac9a02e19" "basis" 2103 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-34117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce26831e23d08765ee5e6e3107cbde1d08ad88c5819e10d9cafe4dcac9a02e19" "basis" 2103 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-34117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce26831e23d08765ee5e6e3107cbde1d08ad88c5819e10d9cafe4dcac9a02e19" "basis" 2103 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce26831e23d08765ee5e6e3107cbde1d08ad88c5819e10d9cafe4dcac9a02e19" "basis" 2103 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\nk=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce26831e23d08765ee5e6e3107cbde1d08ad88c5819e10d9cafe4dcac9a02e19" "basis" 2103 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7604223d1ff525b3348731edda4438ac95858e98d15977ecd0b503cd9c307c0e" "basis" 2103 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74558" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce26831e23d08765ee5e6e3107cbde1d08ad88c5819e10d9cafe4dcac9a02e19" "basis" 2103 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74558" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-11"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce26831e23d08765ee5e6e3107cbde1d08ad88c5819e10d9cafe4dcac9a02e19" "basis" 2103 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74558" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-9"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/state.json" "file_sha2