19e10d9cafe4dcac9a02e19" "basis" 2103 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063819/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-34058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-34058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=1.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-1=1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=2\\cdot 1=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-34058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10a3bc15ed12f67b49c5077f5ff71545347ec1e0741ea25a2c8acf3947651739"} {"question" "q-34058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-34058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-34058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-34115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-34115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}=-2 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 31\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=31,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $b$ does *not* lie in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-34115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10a3bc15ed12f67b49c5077f5ff71545347ec1e0741ea25a2c8acf3947651739"} {"question" "q-34115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-34115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-34115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-34218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, ${a}_{3}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-34218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}=6 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3}=-14 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 6 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 6 & -14 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & -14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & -14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}=6 \\\\ {x}_{2}=4 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(-2)=6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+4{a}_{2}+(-2){a}_{3} & =b \\\\ 2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+(-2)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=2\\cdot 4\\cdot (-2)=-16.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-34218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10a3bc15ed12f67b49c5077f5ff71545347ec1e0741ea25a2c8acf3947651739"} {"question" "q-34218" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-34218" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-16"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "-8"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-34218" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-16"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-34117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, ${a}_{3}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-34117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+6{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-9 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 18 & -21 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-18{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+6{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+6(-1)=-4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+(-3){a}_{2}+(-1){a}_{3} & =b \\\\ 2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+(-3)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+(-1)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=2\\cdot (-3)\\cdot (-1)=6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-34117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10a3bc15ed12f67b49c5077f5ff71545347ec1e0741ea25a2c8acf3947651739"