9" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-74559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}=-8 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+10{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 9 & -8 \\\\ -2 & 10 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 10 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 6 & k+6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-6{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-18\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-18.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-18\\,⇒\\,k=18.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256