-74560" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ -10 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}=-12 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2}=-10 \\\\ -6{x}_{1}+18{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-3 & 9 & -12 \\\\ -2 & 7 & -10 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 7 & -10 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+24\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+24.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+24\\,⇒\\,k=-24.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-74560" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10a3bc15ed12f67b49c5077f5ff71545347ec1e0741ea25a2c8acf3947651739"} {"question" "q-74560" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-74560" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-18"] ["math" "-20"] ["math" "-24"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-74560" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-24"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-74597" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-74597" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 12 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & k+6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{6}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & k+6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+4.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+4\\,⇒\\,k=-4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-74597" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10a3bc15ed12f67b49c5077f5ff71545347ec1e0741ea25a2c8acf3947651739"} {"question" "q-74597" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-74597" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-74597" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-105253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,3,2⟩$, $c=⟨2,-1,-1⟩$, and  $u=⟨5,-5,-4⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-105253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-s+2t=5 \\\\ 3s-t=-5 \\\\ 2s-t=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-s+2t=5 \\\\ t=2 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+2t & =5 \\\\ -s+2(2) & =5 \\\\ -s+4 & =5 \\\\ s & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-1,\\,t=2,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-b+2c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-1)\\cdot 2=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-105253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10a3bc15ed12f67b49c5077f5ff71545347ec1e0741ea25a2c8acf3947651739"} {"question" "q-105253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-105253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-105253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-105248" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,-4,2⟩$, $c=⟨3,-10,2⟩$, and  $u=⟨-2,5,0⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-105248" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s+3t=-2 \\\\ -4s-10t=5 \\\\ 2s+2t=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -10 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=-2,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $s$ and $t$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc=u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $u$ does *not* lie on the plane $Π.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-105248" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10a3bc15ed12f67b49c5077f5ff71545347ec1e0741ea25a2c8acf3947651739"} {"question" "q-105248" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-105248" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-18"] ["math" "-9"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "6"] ["text" "$u$ does not lie on $Π$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-105248" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$u$ does not lie on $Π$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-74598" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,2,3⟩$, $c=⟨3,-7,-9⟩$, and  $u=⟨2,-3,-6⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-74598" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-s+3t=2 \\\\ 2s-7t=-3 \\\\ 3s-9t=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -7 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -9 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -9 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-s+3t=2 \\\\ -t=1 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-t=1\\,⟹\\,t=-1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+3t & =2 \\\\ -s+3(-1) & =2 \\\\ -s & =5 \\\\ s & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-5,\\,t=-1,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-5b-c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-5)\\cdot (-1)=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-74598" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10a3bc15ed12f67b49c5077f5ff71545347ec1e0741ea25a2c8acf3947651739"} {"question" "q-74598" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-74598" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "5"] ["text" "$u$ does not lie on $Π$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-74598" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-105261" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,-1,3⟩$, $c=⟨-2,4,-3⟩$, and  $u=⟨3,-7,3⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-105261" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s-2t=3 \\\\ -s+4t=-7 \\\\ 3s-3t=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s-2t=3 \\\\ t=-2 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=-2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s-2t & =3 \\\\ s-2(-2) & =3 \\\\ s+4 & =3 \\\\ s & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-1,\\,t=-2,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-b-2c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-1)\\cdot (-2)=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-105261" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10a3bc15ed12f67b49c5077f5ff71545347ec1e0741ea25a2c8acf3947651739"} {"question" "q-105261" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-105261" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-105261" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-34212" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,7,-3⟩$, $c=⟨-8,10,-4⟩$, and  $u=⟨6,9,-4⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-34212" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s-8t=6 \\\\ 7s+10t=9 \\\\ -3s-4t=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 10 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 66 & -33 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 66 & -33 \\\\ 0 & -28 & 14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{66}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & -28 & 14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+28{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s-8t=6 \\\\ t=-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s-8t & =6 \\\\ s-8(-\\frac{1}{2}) & =6 \\\\ s+4 & =6 \\\\ s & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=2,\\,t=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=2b-\\frac{1}{2}c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-34212" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10a3bc15ed12f67b49c5077f5ff71545347ec1e0741ea25a2c8acf3947651739"} {"question" "q-34212" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-34212" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "2"] ["text" "$u$ does not lie on $Π$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "q-34212" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/state.json" "file_sha256" "b09952452ba340fbb998c3a10368701b3a576e81c1b0b6896215a4d60fd8d86d"} {"question" "e-4795" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine if $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\},$ where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/assets/df4f126da2ab3a0661bcb7dc18bb1e5eae8cd48d5c5a1464ea580ccc439195d6.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/example-4795.json" "file_sha256" "fe90e6f2720091c87336fc3872fe2e0f65abfb8bd7474dd4e986ce12da403562"} {"question" "e-4795" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}$ if there exist $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=8 \\\\ {x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -21\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -21\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+8{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0x_1 + 0x_2 = 3,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $\\mathbf{b}$ does *not* lie in $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/example-4795.json" "file_sha256" "fe90e6f2720091c87336fc3872fe2e0f65abfb8bd7474dd4e986ce12da403562"} {"question" "e-6218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\},$ where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/assets/399d7fed8338969b654454d30f2ee661edbd52b3a61d065f33972be21996e188.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/example-6218.json" "file_sha256" "2ddfbc74cfa2f4043cab51766ee779c99136c1d179131f186accacab387a3191"} {"question" "e-6218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}$ if there exist $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=13 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ 7{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 2 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 14 & -70 \\\\ 7 & 2 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 14 & -70 \\\\ 0 & 16 & k-91\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{14}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 16 & k-91\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-16{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0x_1 + 0x_2 = k-11$. Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0 = k-11 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad k=11.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/example-6218.json" "file_sha256" "2ddfbc74cfa2f4043cab51766ee779c99136c1d179131f186accacab387a3191"} {"question" "e-4799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine if the vector $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\;\\Pi \\,:\\, \\mathbf{r}=s \\mathbf{b} + t \\mathbf{c}, \\, t,s \\in \\mathbb{R},$ where  $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 1, 4, 5 \\rangle, \\mathbf{c} = \\langle 2, 4, 6 \\rangle$ and  $\\mathbf{u}= \\langle 2, 10, 12 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/example-4799.json" "file_sha256" "e140477fcf0adf115d2f2c51e9814055491c3372f88f6c15241dc186e5220262"} {"question" "e-4799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By definition, $\\mathbf{u} \\in \\Pi$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s+2t=2 \\\\ 4s+4t=10 \\\\ 5s+6t=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 10 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s+2t=2 \\\\ -4t=2 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-4t = 2 \\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad t = -\\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s+2t & =2 \\\\ s+2(-\\frac{1}{2}) & =2 \\\\ s-1 & =2 \\\\ s & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=3, \\, t=-\\dfrac{1}{2},$ we conclude that $\\mathbf{u}$ does indeed lie on the plane $\\Pi.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}=3\\mathbf{b} - \\dfrac{1}{2}\\mathbf{c}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/example-4799.json" "file_sha256" "e140477fcf0adf115d2f2c51e9814055491c3372f88f6c15241dc186e5220262"}] "usage" {"q-34117" [] "e-4799" [] "e-4795" [] "e-6218" [] "q-105208" [] "q-74560" [] "q-74558" [] "q-34115" []} "basis" 2864 "retractions" [[17592186